  "body": "Refs #5119 (remainder). Queue task 14074. Fixes the unresolved P2 from PR #8356's review (discussion r4532341753).\n\n## Problem\n\nSlice 3 (PR #8356) persisted server-config provisioning into `directory.jsonl` beside the groups log. But a durable world loads its directory from `.id-worlds/<name>/directory.jsonl` (`world_store::open_world`), and nothing ever passed the provisioned accounts into that directory. Serving a durable world with `--server-config` therefore reported successful account provisioning at startup while the live world's directory view (`directory_view.rs`) treated the configured keys as anonymous.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `Provisioned::apply_users` is extracted from `Provisioned::apply` (behaviour-preserving: `apply` now calls it first, then the group loop, with identical report semantics). This lets a directory that is not the provisioning home receive the same accounts without taking the group events, which belong to the groups log.\n- `cmd_serve`, after the config load and fail-fast provisioning, seeds the **default** world's directory (the world serve opens at startup) via the new `seed_world_directory` helper whenever world serving is on and the serve is not ephemeral. Seeding is the same idempotent account application, so a restart creates nothing and reports nothing new.\n- Ephemeral worlds hold no directory file, so there is nothing to seed; their state is in-memory and ends with the process, like the world itself. Worlds other than the default open lazily and are not seeded — the config's accounts are server-level identities, and the default world is the serving world the P2 scenario describes.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New regression test `seed_world_directory_provisions_configured_accounts`: seeds a temp world directory from a two-user config, reopens it the way `world_store::open_world` does, asserts both accounts resolve, and asserts a second seed creates nothing.\n- Local verification (laptop, `--no-default-features --features world`, lib tests): `commands::serve::tests::` **47/47 pass** (incl. the slice-3 restart test and the pull-policy tests) and `server_config::` **57/57 pass**. Full default-feature suite is CI's verdict.\n\n## Deliberately not in this PR\n\nThe last #5119 remainder — wiring `ServerConfig::freshness()` into a seitan admission check that serve runs — has no consumer to wire into yet: `seitan::Invite::admit` takes the window as a parameter and has no production caller, and no serving path receives a seitan proof today. That remainder is being explicitly re-scoped on #5119 (it needs a serving admission path designed first), rather than being silently dropped or stubbed here.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796954495&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8413&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8413&signature=a323ffb01690958f38b5bb32fd0480fa1608023b94602cd22a9f47230facd86a\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8413?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
